# 🔐 Password Strength Checker

A simple Python tool that evaluates the strength of a password based on common security criteria.

## 📌 Overview

This project analyzes a password and determines whether it is Weak, Moderate, or Strong based on:

* Length
* Use of uppercase letters
* Use of lowercase letters
* Numbers
* Special characters

## 🚀 Features

* Real-time password strength feedback
* Clear and simple logic
* Beginner-friendly implementation
* Lightweight and fast

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

* Python 3

## 📂 How It Works

The script checks for:

* Minimum length (8+ characters)
* Presence of uppercase and lowercase letters
* Inclusion of digits
* Inclusion of special characters

Each condition increases the password strength score.

## ▶️ How to Run

1. Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/password-strength-checker.git
```

2. Navigate into the folder:

```bash
cd password-strength-checker
```

3. Run the script:

```bash
python password_checker.py
```

